### ERP Simulator — manual test requests
# Works in Visual Studio, Rider and VS Code (REST Client extension): click "Send Request" above each block.
# Start the stack first: docker compose up -d --build
#
# Every POST gets a seeded random behavior, so the same request may return 202, 429 or 500 on different calls.
# Watch the chosen behavior live: docker compose logs -f erp-simulator

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@invoiceNumber = INV-2026-0001

### 1) Submit an invoice (202 / 429 / 500, or 202 after 30s)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoiceNumber": "{{invoiceNumber}}",
  "customerCode": "C-001",
  "amount": 1250.50,
  "currency": "TRY",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-09-29"
}

### 2) Look up the invoice (200 with ERP reference(s), or 404 if it was never saved)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceNumber}}

### 3) Look up an invoice that does not exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/DOES-NOT-EXIST

### 4) Duplicate: send the same invoice number again, then run request 2 — recordCount grows, each record has its own ERP reference
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoiceNumber": "{{invoiceNumber}}",
  "customerCode": "C-001",
  "amount": 1250.50,
  "currency": "TRY",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-09-29"
}

### 5) Invalid body (400, rejected before a behavior is drawn, so the seeded sequence is not affected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoiceNumber": "",
  "customerCode": "C-001",
  "amount": -5,
  "currency": "lira",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-09-29"
}

### 6) The invoice's decision: the lookup also returns decision (none, received, approved, rejected), reason and decided_at
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceNumber}}

### 7) The records received in a time range, one page at a time ([from, to), pageSize at most 500)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices?from=2026-10-05T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-06T00:00:00Z&page=1&pageSize=100

### 8) Page size above 500 is a 400 (not cut)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices?from=2026-10-05T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-06T00:00:00Z&pageSize=501

### 9) OpenAPI document (also browsable at {{baseUrl}}/swagger)
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
